      "title": "Western states lead vehicle sales in July-September quarter: Siam",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/auto/western-states-lead-vehicle-sales-in-july-september-quarter-siam-126111800715_1.html",
      "description": "Maharashtra recorded the highest passenger vehicle sales among Indian states and Union Territories in the July-September quarter, while Uttar Pradesh led in two-wheelers and three-wheelers, according to data from the Society of Indian Automobile Manufacturers (SIAM).\nPassenger vehicle sales across the country totalled 13.61 lakh units in the second quarter of fiscal 2026-27, the industry body said. Maharashtra accounted for 1,65,000 units, or 12.1 per cent of the total, followed by Uttar Pradesh, Gujarat, Tamil Nadu and Karnataka.\nTwo-wheelers, India's largest vehicle segment by volume, saw sales of 64.33 lakh units in the quarter. Uttar Pradesh led with 7,89,000 units, or 12.3 per cent of the total, ahead of Maharashtra, Tamil Nadu, Gujarat and Karnataka.\nBy zone, the western region led in three of the four segments: passenger vehicles (4,29,000 units), two-wheelers (2.113 million) and commercial vehicles (1,13,000). The southern region led in three-wheelers with 96,000 ...",
